## 📝 **NOTES & DECISIONS**

### **Architecture Decisions**
- All managers follow singleton pattern with EventEmitter
- Configuration management is centralized and versioned
- Event-driven communication between managers
- Repository separation between system and product governance
- Git governance follows conventional commits and quality gates
- Environment governance provides proactive configuration management

### **Technical Debt**
- Test script needs improvement (see immediate priority)
- Some linter errors need resolution
- Documentation needs updating for new managers
- File management system successfully implemented and operational
- Git governance system requires team training and adoption

### **Risk Mitigation**
- Regular backups of configuration and data
- Comprehensive testing before deployments
- Rollback procedures for all changes
- Monitoring and alerting for critical systems
- Quality gates prevent poor code from reaching production
- Branch protection ensures code review requirements

